# Fallback mitigation for the phantom KEY_MICMUTE device on HONOR MagicBook
# laptops with the FocalTech FTSC1000 touchscreen (I2C HID 2808:5662).
#
# The touchscreen declares a vendor-defined collection on HID usage page
# 0xff01, which the kernel unconditionally maps to KEY_MICMUTE because that
# page belongs to HP's hotkey usages. hid-multitouch exports it as a second
# input device, named "... UNKNOWN", whose only key is KEY_MICMUTE. It ends up
# stuck down and auto-repeating, which is what makes the microphone mute and
# unmute on its own.
#
# The proper fix is the rebuilt hid-multitouch module installed by install.sh
# in this directory, which stops the phantom device from being created at all.
# This rule is for machines that cannot build kernel modules. It only tells
# libinput to ignore the device: the kernel still generates the events and
# still burns ~30 wakeups per second on the auto-repeat timer, and anything
# reading evdev directly still sees them.
#
# Install: cp to /etc/udev/rules.d/ then
#   sudo udevadm control --reload-rules && sudo udevadm trigger

ACTION=="add|change", SUBSYSTEM=="input", ATTRS{id/vendor}=="2808", \
  ATTRS{id/product}=="5662", ATTRS{name}=="*UNKNOWN*", \
  ENV{LIBINPUT_IGNORE_DEVICE}="1"
